hey this is preshtalwalker  this is a problem that many people  cannot correctly solve  a man buys a horse for sixty dollars  he sells the horse for seventy dollars  he then buys the horse back for eighty  dollars  and he sells the horse again for ninety  dollars  in the end how much money did the man  make or lose  or did he break even  give this problem a try and when you're  ready keep watching the video for the  solution  the short answer is the man made a  profit of twenty dollars  he made ten dollars each of the two  times he sold the horse  this is a total of twenty dollars profit  we can also see this by tracking his net  cash position  the first transaction he buys the horse  for sixty dollars  so he's out  sixty dollars this is negative sixty  dollars  relative to a starting point  he sells the horse for 70 so he then  gets plus 70  which results in a cash position of plus  10 from where he started  he then buys a horse back for eighty  dollars so he needs to spend eighty  dollars which is negative eighty dollars  so his net position is negative seventy  dollars  he finally sells the horse again for  ninety dollars which means he gets  ninety dollars  and the negative seventy plus ninety is  equal to plus twenty  in the end he makes twenty dollars  did you figure it out  thanks for watching this video please  subscribe to my channel i make videos on  math and game theory you can catch me on  my blog mind your decisions which you  can follow on facebook google plus and  patreon you can catch me on social media  at preshtalwalker and if you like this  video please check out my books there  are links in the video description
 

